1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,104
My watch vibrates at midnight, flashing a number that makes my stomach completely drop to the floor.

2
00:00:07,404 --> 00:00:13,164
Four thousand steps. But I haven't left my apartment all day long. Not even for coffee.

3
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:19,776
Then I remember the subway platform this morning. The man who tripped, dropping his heavy briefcase.

4
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:26,580
Everyone walked right past him. And so did I. My feet kept moving without missing a beat.

5
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:32,352
I look down at the screen again. The label above the number changes right before my eyes.

6
00:00:32,652 --> 00:00:38,988
It doesn't track distance. It tracks retreat. Every step away from someone who needed help.

7
00:00:39,288 --> 00:00:45,024
My phone lights up with a local news alert. A robbery happened at that exact subway stop.

8
00:00:45,324 --> 00:00:51,036
If I had stopped, I could have stopped it. Four thousand steps of pure cowardice.

9
00:00:51,336 --> 00:00:57,816
The watch vibrates again. A brand new number appears, ticking upward as I stand here shaking.

10
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:03,804
Another crisis happening right now across town. When will you finally take a step forward?
